Z||000004||mrfiero||11-18-2001||03:09 PM||||Those pics you posted are when (in my opinion) the Obsession was at its finest.  Pictures of that paint job do not do it any justice......it was something that had to be seen in person.  <P>Now John has painted it a disgusting dark purple/brownish color and made it a targa.  The targa idea I like, but the paint job is not nearly as nice as the "constellation" paint scheme in the above pictures.<P>It used to have a small block Chevy in the back, but now it has a Cadillac Northstar......I believe he was one of the first people to install one in a Fiero.<P>John has won numerous awards with this car and I wouldn't be surprised if it looks different again.  The first time I saw it was in 1994 at the national show in Indianapolis.  It was white and was in a fender bender in the hotel parking lot.......it was after this incident that he repainted it as it looks in the pics above.<P>At any rate, it is a nice car, but I hope he gets rid of the nasty paint color it now has!<p>[This message has been edited by mrfiero (edited 11-18-2001).]||||reg||1
