Z||000012||Monkeyman||11-19-2001||02:31 AM||||It's still purple.  And it still has that awesome motor.  Last I knew John was planning yet another round of modifications.  I'm not sure he can do to it that hasn't been done, but he'll find a way to do something else.  He had planned on selling Obsession and starting on a wildly customized pickup, then another Fiero, but since he didn't get the car sold it's back to working on this one.  I may have to make a trip up to N. Manchester one of these days soon and see just what he's up to.  I don't like the end result of all of his mods, but he's hugely talented.||||reg||1
Z||000013||mrfiero||11-19-2001||12:41 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Monkeyman:<BR><B>  He had planned on selling Obsession and starting on a wildly customized pickup, then another Fiero, but since he didn't get the car sold it's back to working on this one.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>That car has been on sale forever!  When I saw it in 1996 (at the national show in Indy) he had it for sale.  I think he was asking $25,000 for it then, which was a steal, but I didn't have that much $$.<P>Oh well.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
